---
title: Butter Chicken
image: https://saltedmint.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Indian-Butter-Chicken-recipe-with-rice.jpg
time required: 1 hour
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a03U45jFxOI
servings: 4
cuisine: Indian
---

== Butter Chicken ==

In a #bowl, mix @chicken breast{3/4%lbs}(boneless, cubed or sliced) with @ginger paste{1%tbsp}, @garlic paste{1%tbsp}, @red chili powder{1%tbsp}, and @salt{1/8%tsp}.

Marinate for at least ~{15-20%minutes}.

Add some @oil{} to a #pan on medium-high heat and fry the chicken pieces. Set the chicken aside in another #bowl to be kept warm.

> You can use paneer instead of chicken for Butter Paneer, but you may want to add 1 tbsp neutral oil if you do.

== Gravy ==

In the same pan, add a little more @oil{} and add @onion{1/4%lbs}(roughly cut) and @butter{1%spoonful}.

Once onions are cooked, add @tomatoes{1.1%lbs}(roughly diced) and @cashew nuts{50%grams}.

Once mixed, add @water{1/2%cup}, @garlic paste{1%tbsp}, @salt{1/4tsp}, @malt vinegar{2%tbsp}(can replace with 1.5 tbsp white vinegar), @sugar{3%tbsp}, @garam masala powder{1/2%tsp}, and @kashmiri chili powder{2%tbsp}. Evenly mix and then let simmer for at least ~{15-20%minutes}, until the entire thing is mushy. If it gets too dry, add more water as needed.

Turn off heat for pan and transfer to #food processor{} and churn into a fine puree. Strain back into the same pan using a #fine mesh sieve{}, making sure to scrape carefully to avoid food wastage.

Start reheating the mixture. Add @butter{6 tbsp}, @heavy cream{3 tbsp}, @kasoori meethi{1%tsp}, and chicken.

Let simmer for ~{5-7%minutes}. Garnish with fresh heavy cream and kasoori meethi.

